# How long each segment of enus lasts.
#
# A duration is not a property of a segment, so the key is longer than
# the segment table's: unit, left, right, stress, onset, coda, syl, nsyl, fromend, prev, next, nexton.
# Then the length in milliseconds and the pieces it is built out of,
# which are the spans of its formant breakpoints. A line with a
# parameter named after the pieces is that parameter's own split,
# which differs for two segments in five: one formant stops at the
# segment's end and another runs on past it, having no target there.
#
# Written by tools/module/durations.py. See docs/authoring.md.
